## Why RAG Instead of Alternatives?

| Approach | Fresh data? | Cost | Hallucination control | Source attribution |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Fine-tuning** | No — retrain to update | High | Weak | None |
| **Long context** (paste everything) | Yes | Very high per call, slow | OK | Hard |
| **RAG** | Yes — re-index a doc in seconds | Low (only relevant chunks sent) | Strong ("answer only from context") | Built-in (you know which chunks were used) |

That last column matters a lot in production: because *you* selected the chunks, you can show the user **citations** ("source: HR Handbook, p. 12") and let them verify. That's a huge trust win for a business chatbot.

